    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Structure**\n- `cmd/server/main.go` — reads `DATABASE_URL` (no hardcoded credentials), connects via `pgxpool`, applies migrations, serves on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- `internal/api/api.go` — chi v5.2.1 router with all four endpoints, URL/code validation, crypto-random code generation\n- `internal/store/store.go` — pgx persistence layer with atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING` click counting\n- `internal/migrate/` — embedded SQL migrations tracked in a `schema_migrations` table, applied in transactions at startup\n- `start.sh` — builds from vendored deps (offline-safe, falls back to prebuilt `bin/server`), then runs the server in the foreground; migrations apply before serving\n\n**Verification results** (all against a live server via `sh start.sh`):\n- `POST /links` → 201 with `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`, URL returned byte-for-byte unchanged (query/fragment preserved); auto-generated and custom codes both work; `code: null` treated as omitted\n- Duplicate custom code → 409; missing/invalid URL, invalid code (bounds checked at 4 and 20 chars), malformed/empty body, non-string URL → 422\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200, unknown → 404 JSON\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with correct `Location`; unknown → 404; 20 parallel redirects produced exactly 20 clicks (atomic single-statement increment)\n- `GET /links` → ascending creation order, `{\"items\":[...],\"total\":n}`, empty DB returns `{\"items\":[],\"total\":0}`\n- Persistence: killed and restarted the server — links and click counts survived; also dropped all tables and confirmed migrations re-apply cleanly on a fresh database\n- `go vet` and `gofmt` clean; chi stays pinned at v5.2.1\n\nThe test server has been stopped, so port 8000 is free for the grading run."
